# std/import-source (design/caos-expr.md): an entry for an OPERATION OF THE STEP. `@op`
# says llm-step does the work in process (it owns the call's lifecycle: it pins the
# remote observation before anything is transferred, then attaches the source tree),
# so this entry exists to give the operation a path, a help and a place in
# `tool_help`/`run_tool`. The image it curries is never run.
HELP=<<END
Import an HTTPS Git repository as a new, unchanged snapshot at an unused conversation path. Returns its full commit hash; preserves its tree and ancestor history. Does not merge or overwrite code. Public repositories need no token. The remote is observed when the call starts, so to see a branch's CURRENT head call this again with a fresh `into`: the new snapshot is how you learn the hash, and the tree you merge from. To import origin/main, select the repository from the chosen source's .source.json provenance and request main; use an explicit repository when ambiguous. Local checkouts use the client's /import command.
@param source HTTPS repository URL, without credentials.
@param [revision] Remote branch, full refs/... name, or full commit hash. Omit for the remote default branch. A new call observes the remote again.
@param into Unused conversation path, such as imports/repo/main-2. Its .source.json sibling must also be free.
@op import-source
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --help=$HELP
